@prefix adv: <https://hexplain.io/ns/audio#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/audio> skos:scopeNote "Use for audio resources, their streams and source metadata. Sampling, encoding and timing aspects carry shared properties."@en .
adv:AudioContainer skos:definition "A containing resource for encoded audio content and associated tracks or metadata."@en .
adv:AudioStream skos:definition "An ordered audio sample stream whose sampling, channel and encoding properties are described separately."@en .
adv:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
adv:MetadataTag skos:definition "A metadata-bearing component carrying descriptive information about an audio work or recording."@en .
adv:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using adv:genre, adv:trackNumber. adv:genre takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). adv:trackNumber takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger)."@en .
adv:StreamShape rdfs:label "Stream Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of adv:AudioStream; subjects using asig:sampleRate. aenc:bitrate takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. aenc:codec takes at most one value; each is an IRI naming an instance of skos:Concept. asamp:bitDepth takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. asamp:componentCount takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. asig:sampleRate takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. atime:duration takes at most one value; each is a literal."@en .
adv:TagShape rdfs:label "Tag Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of adv:MetadataTag; subjects using adv:album, adv:artist, adv:trackNumber, adv:trackTitle. adv:album takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal. adv:artist takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal. adv:trackNumber takes at most one value; each is a number greater than 0. adv:trackTitle takes at most one value; each is an xsd:string literal."@en .
adv:album skos:definition "The album or collection title as text supplied by the source metadata."@en .
adv:artist skos:definition "The artist credit as text supplied by the source metadata; it is not an identified person resource."@en .
adv:axisChannel skos:definition "Deprecated duplicate of dlv:axisBand for audio channels, kept so existing descriptions resolve."@en .
adv:axisSample skos:definition "Deprecated duplicate of dlv:axisTime for successive audio samples, kept so existing descriptions resolve."@en .
adv:genre skos:definition "The genre label as supplied by the source; no universal genre classification scheme is implied."@en .
adv:trackNumber skos:definition "The source's integer ordinal identifying a track within its collection."@en .
adv:trackTitle skos:definition "The title of the audio track as supplied by the source metadata."@en .
